    "restoration_notes": "Large native Amazon canopy tree ideal for long-term forest restoration. Excellent candidate for biodiversity restoration and structural forest recovery. Shade tolerance throughout its life cycle allows integration beneath existing forest canopies. Produces valuable hardwood while maintaining ecological integrity. Wildlife-mediated seed dispersal supports natural regeneration. Because seeds are recalcitrant, restoration nurseries should sow immediately after collection. FYNOS AI should classify Maçaranduba as a flagship late-successional species for restoring mature Amazon forest structure and long-term carbon storage."
